Description: PostGIS spatial extension for Apache Cloudberry (Incubating), @CBDB_BRANCH@ build
 This package provides the PostGIS extension built against an Apache Cloudberry
 (incubating) installation: the extension shared libraries (postgis,
 postgis_raster, ...), their SQL/control files under the Cloudberry
 share/extension directory, and the loader/dumper utilities (shp2pgsql,
 pgsql2shp, raster2pgsql). These co-populate the Cloudberry tree at
 /usr/cloudberry-db (the real directory the apache-cloudberry-db-incubating
 package owns) and therefore do not conflict with it.
 .
 It also bundles the custom geospatial runtime stack the extension was linked
 against — GEOS, PROJ, GDAL and SFCGAL — under /usr/local, along with an
 /etc/ld.so.conf.d entry so the dynamic linker can resolve them (ldconfig is
 run from the maintainer scripts). The package therefore requires only a
 matching Apache Cloudberry installation plus a few base system libraries.
